      {
        "id": "f74-curve-1-source",
        "description": "The printed label fixes the ideal exponential with base 4.5. Every sampled vertex is computed as y=base^x; the shared (0,1) point is hidden, so no answer-bearing marker is added. Source-to-modern limitations: Uniform lattice and clean semantic strokes replace scan noise. Curve labels are horizontal rather than slanted. The plotted domains end at the same complete source-frame bounds or the top-frame intersection; no source-domain extension. Inventory objects are the visible curve strokes and equation label. The hidden vertices referenced by coordinate assertions are renderer construction facts, not extra source point markers.",
